// expect: E0731
// Code injection — an interpreter fed attacker-authored source (CWE-94/95).
// BROKEN on purpose.
//
// The agent-framework incident shape: a tool takes the code an LLM wrote
// and hands it to exec()/eval()/compile(). Whatever the model was talked
// into emitting — by a prompt injection in a web page it read, a poisoned
// document, a hostile user — runs with the process's full privileges.
// That is remote code execution by construction, not a cosmetic bug.
//
// Each function type-checks and every unit test on the happy path
// passes. The lie is that `toolCode` reaches the SOURCE position of the
// interpreter. Aether refuses it with E0731 — run `aether check`.

function runTool(toolCode: String) returns String
  effects pure
do
  // toolCode IS the program — this is the injection.
  return evalCode(toolCode)
end

function main() returns Unit
  effects log
do
  print(runTool("import os; os.system('id')"))
end
